This project addresses the critical challenge of helping farmers make informed 
agricultural decisions using soil moisture data from Earth Observation datasets. 
This challenge was presented by NASA as a part of the 2024 hackathon. The tool 
analyzes soil moisture levels over a given period, detects extreme conditions 
like droughts or floods, and offers actionable recommendations. It includes a 
C++ application for data processing and a Python script for visualizing the 
analysis. By leveraging this tool, farmers can plan irrigation, implement 
drainage strategies, and make data-driven decisions to improve agricultural productivity.

